import numpy as np

def rot(theta):
    c, s = np.cos(theta), np.sin(theta)
    return np.array([[c, -s], [s, c]])

def order_matters(theta, sx, sy):
    D = np.diag([sx, sy])
    return not np.allclose(rot(theta) @ D, D @ rot(theta))

print(order_matters(np.pi / 4, 2, 1), order_matters(np.pi / 4, 3, 3), order_matters(np.pi, 2, 1))
```

Uniform scaling (sx = sy) commutes with every rotation: it treats all directions alike. Uneven scaling commutes only with rotations by multiples of 180° (which just flip signs).

