def power(base, n):
    if n == 0:
        return 1
    return base * power(base, n - 1)

def fast_power(base, n):
    if n == 0:
        return 1
    half = fast_power(base, n // 2)
    result = half * half
    return result * base if n % 2 else result

print(power(2, 10), fast_power(3, 13) == 3**13, fast_power(2, 1000) == 2**1000)
```

`power` makes n + 1 calls (O(n), depth n: 1000 is right at the recursion limit). `fast_power` halves n each time: O(log n), depth about 11 for n = 1000. Same halving idea as binary search.

